<profile version="1.0">
  <!-- Inspections disabled for this Qodana gate (reusable across projects):
       - WeakerAccess: conflicts with ClassEscapesItsScope on public value-object APIs (mutually exclusive)
       - OptionalUsedAsFieldOrParameterType: Optional as a field or parameter type is an accepted pattern
       - ParametersPerConstructor: wide records (many components) are acceptable
       - SystemOutErr: a CLI tool legitimately writes to standard output and error
       - SystemExit: a CLI entry point legitimately sets a process exit code
       - SystemGetenv: reading environment variables in a designated config source is intended
       - MavenModelInspection: flags coordinates the Qodana import cannot resolve (environment noise)
       - XmlHighlighting: flags unregistered XSD schema URIs (environment noise)
       - UnusedProperty: runtime-read config properties look unused to static analysis
       - CheckTagEmptyBody: intentionally empty XML elements are valid
       - unused: whole-program reachability cannot see framework, service-loader, or reflective entry points;
         UnusedSymbol remains enabled for declarations whose unused status is locally provable
       - InstanceVariableInitialization: dependency-injection frameworks initialize fields after construction;
         InstanceVariableUninitializedUse remains enabled for reads that can actually observe an uninitialized field
       - UnnecessaryModuleDependencyInspection: source analysis cannot see dependencies consumed through resources
       - ClassUnconnectedToPackage: a package may legitimately expose one independent API type
       - PackageWithTooManyClasses: many small single-purpose classes per package is the intended design
       - PackageWithTooFewClasses: a package may legitimately hold a single class
       - IfCanBeAssertion: replacing a runtime check with an assert is unsafe (asserts are disabled by default)
       - ClassWithTooManyDependents: penalizes a widely-reused class; many dependents indicate reuse, not a smell
       - PublicInnerClass: conflicts with PackageVisibleInnerClass (an accessible nested class cannot satisfy both)
       - MethodCallInLoopCondition: fires on while (matcher.find()) and every other loop whose condition is
         loop-variant by construction, which is the idiomatic form rather than a smell; the call it asks to hoist
         is the one that advances the loop, so taking the advice would hang the loop
  -->

